<title>BELGIUM: EU seeks beef export refund link to animal welfare.</title>
<headline>EU seeks beef export refund link to animal welfare.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union beef export subsidies should be linked to the respect of animal welfare standards, the European Commission proposed.</p>
<p>The proposal, which is subject to the approval of EU farm ministers, follows pressure from Sweden and other northern EU member states following reports of unacceptable suffering by farm animals being transported long distances.</p>
<p>The Commission has proposed amending EEC Regulation 805/68 on the common beef and veal regime, adding, &quot;...the payment of the refund for exports of live animals is subject to...the protection of animals during transport.&quot;</p>
<p>Detailed implementing rules would be defined by the EU's beef management committee.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
